{"id":16709,"chebi_accession":"CHEBI:16709","name":"pyridoxine","stars":3,"definition":"A hydroxymethylpyridine with hydroxymethyl groups at positions 4 and 5, a hydroxy group at position 3 and a methyl group at position 2. The 4-methanol form of vitamin B<small><sub>6</sub></small>, it is converted intoto pyridoxal phosphate which is a coenzyme for synthesis of amino acids, neurotransmitters, sphingolipids and aminolevulinic acid.","ascii_name":"pyridoxine","names":{"SYNONYM":[{"name":"2-methyl-3-hydroxy-4,5-bis(hydroxymethyl)pyridine","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"2-methyl-3-hydroxy-4,5-bis(hydroxymethyl)pyridine","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"2-Methyl-3-hydroxy-4,5-dihydroxymethyl-pyridin","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"2-Methyl-3-hydroxy-4,5-dihydroxymethyl-pyridin","adapted":false,"language_code":"de"},{"name":"2-methyl-3-hydroxy-4,5-di(hydroxymethyl)pyridine","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"2-methyl-3-hydroxy-4,5-di(hydroxymethyl)pyridine","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"2-methyl-3-hydroxy-4,5-dihydroxymethylpyridine","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"NIST Chemistry WebBook","ascii_name":"2-methyl-3-hydroxy-4,5-dihydroxymethylpyridine","adapted":true,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"2-methyl-4,5-bis(hydroxymethyl)-3-hydroxypyridine","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"2-methyl-4,5-bis(hydroxymethyl)-3-hydroxypyridine","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"2-methyl-4,5-dimethylol-pyridin-3-ol","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChEBI","ascii_name":"2-methyl-4,5-dimethylol-pyridin-3-ol","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"3-hydroxy-2-picoline-4,5-dimethanol","status":"C","type":"SYNONYM","source":"ChemIDplus","ascii_name":"3-hydroxy-2-picoline-4,5-dimethanol","adapted":false,"language_code":"en"},{"name":"3-hydroxy-4,5-bis(hydroxymethyl)-2-methylpyridine","status":"C","